fuxi: 0106 -- netlog: stream the console and take commands over the USB link

The port already enumerates as a CDC-ECM Ethernet device once it boots with
sweethw=1 (ue0, 192.168.7.2/24), but nothing used it: the only way to see a boot
was to photograph the framebuffer, and the only way to ask the kernel anything
was to reboot it with different strings in the payload.

This gives that link a job.  The host's cdc_ether owns the bulk pipe, so rather
than stand up an IP story (DHCP, routes, an in-kernel UDP server) the channel
rides its own ethertype, 0x88B5 ("local experimental"), on the same interface.
The host reads it with an AF_PACKET socket, so nothing needs configuring:

  phone -> host   the console stream.  conslog_putc() taps every character
                  kernel printf() emits into a lock-free 64 KiB ring
                  (bsd/dev/fuxi_netlog.c); a kernel thread drains it into frames
                  of <=1200 bytes.  A panic prints to this too, which is exactly
                  when the screen is useless.
  host -> phone   one text command per frame, handled in the USB receive path
                  before the frame reaches the ethernet stack:
                    help | stat | cpu | log on|off | echo <text>

The tap is lock-free and cannot block: printf holds the OS-log lock and runs in
interrupt context and in panic, so the producer only writes a byte and bumps a
release counter, and the drain thread is the sole consumer.  A full ring drops
the newest byte and counts it, it never loses the framing of what was already
queued.

`fuxinet=0` disables the whole thing; it is on by default only because the USB
link itself is already gated behind sweethw=1.

`cpu` uses the PMCCNTR probe from 0105 (its helper loses its internal linkage so
this can call it), so the answer to 'is it boosting' can be asked over USB
instead of by photographing the screen.

Host side: tools/fuxi-netlog.py (AF_PACKET on the phone's interface, prints the
stream, sends commands).  Kernel side is ~200 lines in one new file plus four
small hooks.  Verified to apply with the series: applied=105 skipped=0.
